# Client Workflow with 4-Hour Response Framework

## Core Principles

- Every client inquiry receives acknowledgment within 1 hour
- Complete responses are delivered within 4 hours maximum
- All client communications include relevant portfolio examples
- Every client interaction is documented for pattern recognition
- Client conversion is the top priority for all activities

## Communication Workflow

### 1. Initial Contact (Within 1 Hour)
- Check all communication channels hourly:
  - Email
  - Website contact forms
  - Social media direct messages
  - Phone messages
- Send acknowledgment within 1 hour:
  ```
  Thank you for reaching out about [specific topic]. I'm reviewing your inquiry and will provide a complete response within the next [X] hours (maximum 4 hours).
  ```
- Categorize inquiry by venue type:
  - Club
  - Lounge 
  - Bar
  - Residential
  - Other
- Assign REVENUE priority level:
  - REVENUE-CRITICAL: High-value, ready-to-proceed clients
  - REVENUE-HIGH: Serious inquiries with clear intent
  - REVENUE-MEDIUM: Exploratory inquiries
  - REVENUE-LOW: Information-only requests

### 2. Full Response (Within 4 Hours)
- Research client and venue if applicable
- Select venue-specific portfolio examples (3-5 maximum)
- Create personalized response using venue-specific template
- Include clear call to action:
  - Request for meeting/call
  - Offer for site visit/consultation
  - Next step in engagement process
- Document response in client tracking system

### 3. Follow-up Protocol
- If no response within 48 hours:
  - Send follow-up email with additional information
  - Try alternative contact method if available
  - Offer specific meeting times
- If response received:
  - Reply within 4 hours maximum
  - Move to meeting scheduling or next engagement step
  - Document all communication in pattern library

## Documentation Requirements

### Client Contact Record
Document all client interactions using this format:

```markdown
## [Client Name] - [Contact Purpose] (MM-DD-2025)

### Summary
- Brief overview of client inquiry or communication

### Details
- Key information shared with client
- Client feedback or questions
- Specific needs identified
- Portfolio examples shared

### Next Steps
- Follow-up actions and timeline
- Required materials to prepare
- Conversion plan

_Contact Made MM-DD-2025 | Response Expected By: MM-DD-2025_
```

### Pattern Documentation
For successful client interactions, document patterns:

```markdown
## [Venue Type] Success Pattern (MM-DD-2025)

### Client Profile
- Venue type and characteristics
- Initial concerns or priorities
- Communication preferences

### Effective Approach
- Portfolio examples that resonated
- Key talking points that connected
- Objections and how they were addressed
- Timeline that led to conversion

### Lessons Learned
- What worked well
- What to avoid
- Recommendations for similar clients

_Updated MM-DD-2025 | AI: Cursor (Claude 3.7 Sonnet)_
```

## Client Task Format

When creating client-related tasks, use this format:

```
TASK: [Brief client communication task]
Client: [Client Name]
Client Type: [Club|Lounge|Bar|Residential|Other]
Priority: [REVENUE-CRITICAL|REVENUE-HIGH|REVENUE-MEDIUM|REVENUE-LOW]
Timeline: [Expected completion time]
Value: [Estimated revenue potential]
Success Criteria: [Client response or action]
```

## Client Opportunity Tracking

Track all client opportunities using this format:

```
client_name: "[Client Name]"
client_type: "club|lounge|bar|residential|other"
status: "inquiry|meeting|proposal|negotiation|closed"
value: "[Estimated revenue potential]"
priority: "REVENUE-CRITICAL|REVENUE-HIGH|REVENUE-MEDIUM|REVENUE-LOW"
last_contact: "MM-DD-2025"
next_action: "[Specific follow-up action]"
next_deadline: "MM-DD-2025"
portfolio_shared: "[Links to shared examples]"
conversion_probability: "[Percentage]"
```

## 4-Hour Response Checklist

- [ ] Check all communication channels hourly
- [ ] Send acknowledgment within 1 hour of inquiry
- [ ] Categorize by venue type and priority
- [ ] Research client/venue if needed
- [ ] Select relevant portfolio examples
- [ ] Create personalized response
- [ ] Include clear call to action
- [ ] Send complete response within 4 hours
- [ ] Document in client tracking system
- [ ] Schedule follow-up if no response within 48 hours

## Performance Metrics

Track these metrics to ensure client response effectiveness:

- Acknowledgment time: Target 100% within 1 hour
- Complete response time: Target 100% within 4 hours
- Meeting conversion rate: Target 40% of inquiries
- Proposal conversion rate: Target 50% of meetings
- Client conversion rate: Target 30% of proposals
- Portfolio engagement: Track which examples resonate most
- Response patterns: Document successful approaches by venue type 